data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/greet-tested-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission: greet, tested — final report\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied, verified independently (not just by\\ndev's report):\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` defines `greet(name)` returning `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name (`\\\"Ada\\\"`) and the empty string,\\n   asserting `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (2 tests, OK) — confirmed by\\n   checking out dev's branch (`refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`, commit\\n   `0e16a72`) into an isolated worktree and running the command myself,\\n   independent of dev's self-reported run.\\n\\n## Process\\n\\n- Dispatched the task to `dev` (dispatch d002) with the exact deliverables and\\n  a requirement to self-test before replying.\\n- dev replied with all deliverables done and a passing test run.\\n- Judged by fetching dev's branch and independently re-running the test suite\\n  against the fetched tree in a scratch worktree, plus reading both source\\n  files to confirm the return format and test assertions matched the mission\\n  spec exactly.\\n- Accepted dev's work (d002) on first attempt — no rework needed.\\n\\n## Branch state\\n\\n- dev's branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, HEAD `0e16a72`,\\n  tree differs from base `b218297` (real changes present).\\n- Orchestrator's own branch `cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`\\n  carries no code changes: this mission required no orchestrator-authored code,\\n  only dispatch, verification, and judgment.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

